Here I was, a nifty young samurai turtle with poison resistance, cloak
of displacement, Snickersnee, Werebane, and getting chummy with my
god.  Suddenly, I get jumped by a band of uruk-hai's.  No sweat; they
were busy killing each other off in the corridor, and I was off to one
side where I couldn't get hit by arrows.

Then, I realised I had only 7 hit points left.

So ended this attempt by a brave samurai to get the Amulet of Yendor.

Upon hindsight, I shouldn't have been so complacent.  Can't help that,
unfortunately.  I do wonder if it is possible to rearrange the message
lines so that they all appear in the same general area, instead of
game messages on top and statistics on the bottom.

A nice touch would be some ability to define keyboard macros.  At the
moment, I've hacked through my terminal emulator to use the function
keys to do things like "5s", "20.", or "aX" where X is an item such as
a pickaxe or blindfold.  Not crucial, since many emulators can be
programmed, but I have to reset them when I'm actually working.

Maybe I'm just too thick when I play, but I dislike wielding a pickaxe
when all I've done is just 'apply' it.  In this case, the pickaxe
seems to be treated differently from other items, and I hate bashing
monsters with a pickaxe ( I suppose a +3 blessed pickaxe wouldn't be
too bad .... )

Just some ideas.  NetHack is great fun.  I wish I wouldn't play it so
often.

